achability entirely (step_10), showing the result depends on actual event timing, not mere static connectivity. 883's only in-neighbours are 729 and 1209 (step_11), so the 729->883 hop is the genuine delivery step rather than one of many. Global activity peaks in the last bin (step_12), away from the cascade window, so the chain is not simply riding a burst."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_2ff9db1a\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 66, 1952, 1090, 729, 883],\n  \"window\": [65717, 75317],\n  \"confidence\": 0.89,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"A concrete time-respecting chain exists: 1010->66 (t=70051), 66->1952 (70204), 1952->1090 (70407), 1090->729 (70753), 729->883 (70983). Times strictly increase and the largest inter-hop gap is 346 units, well under the 600-unit limit (step_01, step_05); each hop is a real directed edge (step_07, step_08). Confounder checks: the relay nodes are not hubs \u2014 1010, 883, 66, 1952, 1090, 729 each have only 3-5 events and no repeated edges in the window (step_03, step_04), and none appear among the top-10 most active nodes (step_06), so the path is not an artifact of high-volume popular nodes in a sparse graph (repeat ratio 0.0085, step_02). Directionality/ordering matters: the reverse cascade 883->1010 is unreachable (step_09), and truncating the window before t=70051 destroys reachability entirely (step_10), showing the result depends on actual event timing, not mere static connectivity. 883's only in-neighbours are 729 and 1209 (step_11), so the 729->883 hop is the genuine delivery step rather than one of many. Global activity peaks in the last bin (step_12), away from the cascade window, so the chain is not simply riding a burst.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 27629, "total_output_tokens": 2741, "total_tokens": 30370, "total_latency_ms": 43555, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "tool_protocol_errors": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}